--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
libgweather (the C library)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The crate above is a thin wrapper. The code that parses Locations.xml, computes
great-circle distances and renders condition strings is GNOME's C library, which
gweather-sys locates with pkg-config and which the built extension links.

  https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libgweather
  Copyright 1999-2026 the GWeather authors
  Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later

This is recorded here rather than left to be discovered. The LGPL is copyleft;
the Apache License this gem is distributed under is not. The two coexist because
the extension links libgweather-4 dynamically, which is the arrangement LGPL
section 6 exists to permit: the library stays separately replaceable, this gem
stays Apache-2.0, and a user may swap their system libgweather for another build
of it.

Static linking would not be that arrangement, and nothing here should be changed
to do it before the licence question is answered. The Locations.xml database is
distributed with that C library under its terms, and is not redistributed by this
gem.

